{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>If a matter is too extraordinary for you.</b> Even though you have appointed judges in every city, so that each court may judge its own city — yet when a doubt arises as to how the law was received by oral tradition, the court of that city shall not decide it according to their own reasoning, but the ruling shall be according to the reasoning of the majority of the Great Court. And likewise when these do not outweigh those."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 17, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:21:39.012084476Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}